#- §6╔═.✵.════════╗
§5       Witch Hunt!
§6╚════════.✵.═╝
§8The witches of Craftadia (the bad ones) wrote in to tell their side of the story. One witch came by The Spyglass Tavern for an interview. “Do you ever wonder why we wake up and chose violence?" she said as
#- §8she threw a potion at my dog. “We were once peaceful, before you lot showed up, hunting us down, taking our cats, raiding our swamp huts!” Hunting witches is a very common practice in the land, ever since the mysterious Quest Giver decided to reward people for un-aliving multiple at a
#- §8time. “We live in the worst environment ever and our homes are the ugliest buildings ever, it’s cold and miserable, yet people still manage to find us. ”I picked my next words carefully. “Umm.. maybe it’s because of all that cackling, you can hear it from miles away”.
#- §8Another potion burst into my face, making me ill for 45 seconds. “Sorry, please continue”. As we talked deep into the night, many important topics were explored. That they do indeed all have the same mole on their nose and a monobrow. They love attacking people as a hobby and would still
#- §8be doing this regardless of the person (she lied before when she said they were peaceful, they were §4NEVER §8peaceful). They hate mushrooms. The sugar is for their tea, witches love tea. It’s “§4not a stick, it’s a wand, you amateurs§8”. And then there was something about an 
#- §8extra top-secret evil witch cult but I fell asleep. I swiftly ended our interview with one final question. “Tell me, is it true that you can’t use a cauldron or open doors?” With this the witch threw one last potion at my feet and disappeared. 
Left behind was a note with the words:
