§2(§oAs previously seen in CraftLife Magazine)
§5-------------------§8⚘      “ᴮᵉ ᵍᵉⁿᵘⁱⁿᵉ 
    ˡⁱᵏᵉ ᶠᵉʳⁿ ⁱⁿ ᵗʰᵉ ᶠᵒʳᵉˢᵗ” 
        ⁻ ᵁⁿᵏⁿᵒʷⁿ         ⚘
§5-------------------
§2The mystical town of FERN is named after the timeless collection of Craftadian stories
#- §2of a brave adventurer. Her story echoes through the deepest caves and whistles through the tallest trees. Some will believe them to be nothing but a myth, a fairy tale, some old folklore passed through generations.  It is a long and forgotten history for those who travel
#- §2these lands currently. Any valid record of the events that took place many centuries ago could only be told truthfully by those who were there. And it will most definitely be lost in time again, as all things do. So it’s fortunate, dear reader, that powerful witches' such as myself can live for a 
#- §2very long time...

Nature is not human-hearted, but then Fern took her first breath.

A brand new form of life had just been created and the first settlers in the wasteland of Craftadia had been granted a very
#- §2special gift. She was grown from a single sapling. The last sapling. Planted into the earth along with all the hopes of an entire village of lost souls who desperately needed the tree for it’s resources. As we all know too well, in this world, your adventure begins with a single tree.
#- §2The villagers were understandably shocked when they grew a fern instead. A rather strange and unwelcome situation. Deeply saddened by this the villagers turned their prayers upwards toward the heavens, then quickly downward when the ground beneath them started shaking.
#- §2A witch among them had cast a spell on the fern and with a stern voice told the villagers: “§6when the fern blooms at midnight a handful of the seeds should be taken and cast in the air and where they fall shall reveal hidden gold§2”. They had nothing else to lose, and so they waited.
#- §2To be continued…
§5✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿

If you are enjoying this story, you can buy/read a copy from the library at /warp witchbooks ☺ 

