§9 A guide for making a        house a home!  
#- §9   ⛏*⋆§1Article One§9⋆*⛏
§4   ᵀʰᵉ ᴰᵉᵛⁱˡ ᴵˢ ᴵⁿ ᵀʰᵉ ᴰᵉᵗᵃⁱˡ
§8-------------------
§1When it comes to decorating your base and land, it’s often the little touches that can bring that area to life. Instead of blank space, I often enjoy the process of adding everything and anything that can fill it up with a backstory
#- §1of its own. Take my underground or cave builds for example. If I have a house down there I always build it with the idea of nature taking over. Having the roof caving in because of a cave collapse or landslide, bees nests, cobwebs, vines and crates in the spots I never really use or 
#- §1visit that much. Adding roots, mushrooms, plants, and all these awesome lush cave items in dark and gloomy environments can change the mood dramatically. Or if you want dark and gloomy, the odd skull here and there, cobwebs again, minimal lighting along with the moss or cracked stone bricks
#- §1can create a very neglected and dungeon-like atmosphere. Making use of particles and sound effects can push a build to the next level. For example, planting enderchests in the walls or under the floor can make an enchanting, magical feel, a even a more   
#- §1spooky one. Campfires can make smoke either for a cosy fireplace inside the home, a chimney on the outside, an oven for your kitchen or to make the illusion of something being on fire. The new spore blossom (which I’m obsessed with) is the perfect way to make nature-themed builds 
#- §1come alive. If you include dripstone, why not make a small pond, add mud under it or just a tiny puddle underneath, that constant dripping water has to go somewhere right?! 
Pop a nether portal (safely) behind the walls to add a sound effect people won’t expect. 
#- §1Go to that extra effort of adding carpeting to floors or paintings/banners to walls. Try not to stick to the same colour or block type, experiment with a contrast of light blocks against dark blocks, smooth blocks against detailed ones. Putting hay bales and water in for the animals,
#- §1a bed for your doggo, an office desk for you to “do some work”, a library for some light reading, a kitchen area for your many many many furnaces, a tool shed or warehouse instead of a hole (we all do) underground for all your storage needs, a cute little fishing spot complete with real fish
#- §1just so you can complete the fishing quest in style, a pile of logs outside with a small chopping block and axe, small farms or a greenhouse on the surface to disguise the real §4super-mega-massive §1redstone farms under them. All these ideas can make your base explain so much from 
#- §1sight alone. As I said before, a whole backstory can be formed with everything you create having a purpose and meaning. You can use the shape of the land around you to form something that truly feels realistic! 

And fun to relax in and look at! §9Yay \o/
#- §8-------------------
§9⛏§1I’ll dig deeper with ideas like these in the next Crafty Witches!§9⛏
§8-------------------

